    "scope": "Frozen website data plus calculation, filtering, export and build source available at capture.",
    "raw_csv": "Raw CSVs preserve stored fields. Object/array cells use JSON. Null and absent fields are empty CSV cells; use JSON for a lossless distinction. Creativity theme order remains in creativity_papers.json.",
    "joined_learning_csv": "The shared export joins study fields, derives missing CI limits using the captured ciOf helper, and appends metadata and release context. No filtering is applied.",
    "limitations": "Underlying research workbooks, analysis outputs, PDFs and historical paper versions are not bundled or retrospectively verified. This archive reproduces website calculations from its frozen JSON, not extraction from primary documents.",
    "restore": "For calculations and exports, use code/src/shared.mjs with data/*.json; snapshot-tools contains the exact CSV generator and its dependencies. This is not a complete standalone website backup. For the app, copy data/code files to their manifest source_path in a separate directory, copy this entire archive to public/releases/<id>, reconstruct src/release.json from this release's published index entry, and create public/releases/index.json with that entry/current_release_id/schema_version. The reconstructed pointer/index are intentionally outside their own hash manifest to avoid a circular digest. Historical archive lists, PDFs, images and other site assets are not bundled. Install with the archived package-lock.json using npm ci. Do not overwrite a live checkout to reproduce an older release."
  },
